          "text": "{\"occurrence_id\":\"cofield-nikkis-touch-62a21616b980\",\"core_classification\":{\"label_support\":{\"truth_conditional\":4,\"performative\":1,\"exclamatory_reflexive\":0,\"other\":0},\"confidence\":0.96,\"analysis\":\"Franco directly and deliberately avows that he loves Nikki, then explicitly presents the feeling as longstanding and now verified as real. The declaration may carry a weak relational or courtship implication, but it does not clearly undertake a specific commitment. Its measured, reflective presentation provides no independent evidence of expressive/reflex-like discharge.\",\"ambiguity\":\"The declaration may help establish or advance their relationship, giving weak support to P, but the passage primarily frames it as a considered avowal of an emotional state.\"},\"other_diagnosis\":{\"tpe_failure\":null,\"core_not_context\":null},\"utterance_status\":{\"status\":\"direct\",\"description\":\"Franco directly addresses Nikki and says, “I love you, Nikki,” in the narrated scene.\"},\"contextual_interpretation\":\"The hand squeeze, soft emotional expression, whisper, and stated sincerity frame the declaration as intimate and earnest. More decisively, Franco says he has loved Nikki “for a while,” delayed speaking to avoid rushing, and now knows the feeling is real. This makes the utterance a reflective disclosure rather than a reflexive outburst; emotional delivery alone does not establish E.\" ,\"evidence\":[{\"evidence_id\":\"e1\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“I love you, Nikki,” followed by “I’ve loved you for a while now.”\",\"supports\":\"Strong T: Franco explicitly avows a present and continuing loving state.\",\"confidence\":0.99},{\"evidence_id\":\"e2\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"“I needed to make sure I didn’t rush this. But now... I know. I know it’s real.”\",\"supports\":\"The utterance is presented as a considered conclusion after deliberation, supporting T and weighing against expressive/reflexive E.\",\"confidence\":0.98},{\"evidence_id\":\"e3\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"He whispers with a voice described as “steady and sincere,” despite being visibly emotional.\",\"supports\":\"Supports earnest, controlled delivery; the emotional intensity does not independently indicate reflex-like verbal discharge.\",\"confidence\":0.95},{\"evidence_id\":\"e4\",\"source\":\"local_text\",\"quotation_or_description\":\"Franco squeezes Nikki’s hand and addresses her by name during the declaration.\",\"supports\":\"Supports direct interpersonal and courtship significance, with only weak evidence of an enacted relational undertaking.\",\"confidence\":0.85}],\"background_knowledge\":{\"used\":false,\"familiarity\":\"none\",\"confidence\":null,\"contribution\":null},\"ontology_assessment\":{\"fit\":\"natural\",\"diagnosis\":\"T naturally captures the central considered avowal, while a low P score registers its limited relational force. E is unnecessary because deliberation and controlled delivery explain the event without positing expressive/reflexive discharge; no important core force remains outside T/P/E.\",\"candidate_recurrent_dimension\":null},\"notes\":null}"
